messages:
anya: FYI hit a nasty goroutine leak in the go sampleapp when we SIGINT during a streaming generator. process stays alive; pprof points at a blocking token refresh call that never sees ctx cancel.

matt: can you paste the repro?

anya: trimmed sample: 
```go
func runStream(ctx context.Context) error {
  for {
    _, err := client.Generate(ctx, req) // streaming generator API
    if err != nil {
      return err
    }
    // handle tokens
  }
}

func main() {
  ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())
  go func() {
    sig := make(chan os.Signal, 1)
    signal.Notify(sig, os.Interrupt)
    <-sig
    cancel()
  }()
  go authRefresher(ctx) // background refresh loop
  _ = runStream(ctx)
}

func authRefresher(ctx context.Context) {
  for {
    tok := blockingGetToken() // internal http call without ctx
    select {
    case <-time.After(time.Minute): _ = tok
    case <-ctx.Done(): return
    }
  }
}
```

anya: observed: after ctrl-c, runStream returns but process remains; goroutine stuck in blockingGetToken.

sam: yep this is classic: TokenSource implementation blocks and doesn't accept ctx -> leaks.

jenna: long story short: SDK needs a context-aware refresh hook or sample apps must demonstrate safe patterns. We discussed adding Refresh(ctx) on TokenSource and keeping Refresh() for backcompat.

matt: short-term fixes: update sample app to use signal.NotifyContext and make refresh issue http requests with a ctx-aware client; longer-term: add NewContextTokenSource wrapper in SDK that runs refresh with provided ctx.

anya: i'll open a small PR to change sampleapp and add a note in the onboarding README. also filing a ticket for the SDK change.

matt: please add a unit test that simulates a stalled token server (net/http test server that accepts conn and never responds) so CI will catch regressions.

ci-bot: Created ticket RW-4217: "go sdk: context-aware token refresh for long-running streams" and kicked off e2e.

jenna: great. also add a one-liner in generator onboarding checklist: "Ensure token refresh is cancellable when running long-lived streams."

anya: will do, attaching traces + minimal repro in the ticket. thanks for the quick feedback!
